# Report Field Sequence — configurable report columns

## Invariants
- `report_id` (e.g. `RPT-PERF-001`) and `field_key` are **immutable identity** = permission key = audit key. Never rename or reuse them.
- Report Access (`report_access_config`) governs **visibility**. Report Field Sequence governs **column label / order / hide-show only**. The two layers compose — never derive access from a sequence override.
- Master switch: `system_settings.report_overrides_enabled` (jsonb `"false"` default). When OFF, `useResolvedReportFields()` returns defaults and every report renders its hardcoded columns — zero behaviour change.
- DB trigger `report_field_overrides_validate` is the authority: required fields cannot be hidden, non-renamable fields keep their default label, `custom_sort >= 0`. UI mirrors these rules for instant feedback.
- Field keys passed to a report's table cells / exports are stable identifiers; the resolver only changes display label and column order. Pages **must read by `field.field_key`**, never by index.

## Architecture
- `src/lib/reports/catalog.ts` — TS source of truth: `REPORT_CATALOG` seeds `report_registry` + `report_field_registry`. Module prefixes: PERF, INC, KRA, TNI, MAT, EPS, MSR, QRY, ISS, CMP, DEP, AUD, KPID, BNK, KST, KJN, VAR, MTK, TVM, KSD. Helpers `getReportIdFromRoute`, `getRouteFromReportId`.
- `src/lib/reports/applyFieldOverrides.ts` — pure: merges defaults + active overrides → `ResolvedReportField[]`. Sorted ascending by resolved `sort`. `applyAndFilter` strips hidden.
- `src/hooks/useResolvedReportFields.ts` — feature-flag-gated; takes `(reportId, defaults)`, falls back to defaults when registry not seeded or flag off. Admin helpers: `useReportRegistry`, `useReportFieldRegistry`, `useReportFieldOverridesAll`.
- `src/components/admin/ReportFieldSequenceTab.tsx` — admin UI inside System Settings → Report Builder → "Field Sequence" tab. Per-report collapsible card with @dnd-kit sortable column list, inline rename, eye toggle for hide, per-report and global reset, audit-logged save.
- `src/pages/ReportShortlink.tsx` + route `/r/:reportId` — resolves to canonical route (DB lookup with TS catalog fallback) and preserves query string + appends `?rpt=<id>`. 404 view for unknown IDs.
- Wired consumers (XLSX export only — table rendering wiring is per-page follow-up):
  - `RPT-PERF-001` Performance (Phase 4)
  - `RPT-KRA-001` KRA Issuance, `RPT-DEP-001` Department, `RPT-VAR-001` Variance, `RPT-ISS-001` Issues (Phase 5a)
  - `RPT-TNI-001` TNI, `RPT-EPS-001` Employee Performance Summary, `RPT-CMP-001` Completion, `RPT-AUD-001` Audit Trail, `RPT-QRY-001` Query, `RPT-KPID-001` KPI Detail, `RPT-KST-001` KPI Status Tracker, `RPT-BNK-001` Bottleneck (Phase 5b — all Tier A flat-table reports now wired)
  - `RPT-KSD-001` KPI Scorecard Detail (Phase 6a — both single-month and multi-month range exports share the same resolved field set)
  - `RPT-MTK-001` Same KPI — Manager vs Team (Phase 6b)
  - `RPT-TVM-001` Team Vs Manager Monthly Score (Phase 6c)
  - `RPT-KJN-001` KPI Journey Timeline (Phase 6d)
  - `RPT-MSR-001` Monthly Scorecard (Phase 6e — summary export only; PDF and Monthly Trend tab remain hardcoded)
  - `RPT-MAT-001` KPI-Employee Score Matrix (Phase 6f — fixed prefix columns only: Sr.No/Category/KRA/KPI/Weightage/Employee Count. Per-employee `(Wt%)`/`(Score)` columns stay dynamic and are appended after the resolver-driven prefix.)
  - `RPT-INC-001` Incentive Report (Phase 6g — `MonthlyIncentiveTable` XLSX export wired through resolver; 30 fields with employee_code/employee_name/incentive_amount as required. Retroactive Adjustment tab and table UI remain hardcoded.)
  All Tier A + Tier B XLSX exports are now resolver-driven. Remaining hardcoded exports are non-tabular: MSR PDF, MSR Monthly Trend tab, Incentive Retroactive Adjustment tab.

## DB
- `report_registry` — admin write, authenticated read.
- `report_field_registry` — UNIQUE (`report_id`, `field_key`). Admin write, authenticated read.
- `report_field_overrides` — UNIQUE (`report_id`, `field_key`, `COALESCE(client_id,'__global__')`) where `is_active=true`. Soft-delete via `is_active=false`. Admin write, authenticated read.
- `report_field_override_audit` — append-only. `field` ∈ {label, sort, is_hidden, reset}.
- Backup: auto-included via `get_backup_table_order()`.

## Out of scope (deferred)
- Wiring remaining report pages — only Performance is fully wired in Phase 4. Each page wires by adding a `DEFAULT_FIELDS` constant + `useResolvedReportFields(id, DEFAULT_FIELDS)`.
- Per-user (vs per-client) column preferences.
- Adding brand-new fields from the UI (catalog-driven only).
- Multi-tenant `client_id` UI for overrides (column exists, UI stays global).